From e8a2dd9f0b345ea90c4760b255b6cac9072a5ee4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wojtek Mach <wojtek@wojtekmach.pl>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:35:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] erts: Add erlaotc, building executables from releases

erlaotc packages a release directory (lib/ and releases/) into one
executable: the emulator followed by a zip archive of the release, with
the erl arguments in the archive comment. Nothing is extracted at run
time; the code is loaded from the executable as a primary archive
(-primary_archive), read in the calling process. erl_child_setup,
inet_gethost and epmd are linked into the emulator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MVJPWKb8jPWu1ctZmLCcAH
